course: dictionary
lesson: 741
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. The word bat can name an animal, a piece of sports kit, or an action. Context, the words around it, tells you which meaning is right.
explain: «Never touch a bat; some bats carry rabies or similar viruses.» The clues are touch and viruses, so bat is the animal. «Keep a safe distance from anyone swinging a racket or bat, because it can hit your face.» The clues are swinging and hit, so bat is the stick used in games.
explain: Bat can also be a verb. To bat means to take a turn at hitting the ball in a game like cricket. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. If the animal meaning does not fit, try the stick or the action.
explain: The phrase «not bat an eye» is different again. It means to show no surprise at all. Phrases like this do not work word by word, so learn them as a whole.
fact: A bat is a small flying animal with wings of skin that comes out at night.
fact: Bats are mammals, not birds, and most eat insects or fruit.
fact: Many bats find their way with echoes, which is called echolocation. Bats are not blind.
fact: A bat is also a stick or club for hitting the ball in cricket, baseball and rounders.
fact: Bats are protected in many places, so never touch one, because it can carry disease.
exercise: «Never touch a bat; some bats carry rabies or similar viruses.» In this sentence, what is a bat? | A stick for hitting a ball | A type of cricket ball | To take a turn at hitting the ball | *A small flying animal
exercise: «Keep a safe distance from anyone swinging a racket or bat, because it can hit your face.» What is the bat here? | A cave where animals sleep | A bird with skin wings | *A stick or club for hitting the ball | A small animal that flies at night
exercise: What does «not bat an eye» mean? | To fly away quickly | To close one eye on purpose | *To show no surprise | To hit the ball very hard
test: Look at «Bats do not get tangled in people's hair; they are very good at avoiding obstacles.» What is a bat in this sentence? | A club | A verb meaning to take a turn | *An animal | A phrase meaning no surprise
test: Lena had to bat first in the rounders game. What does bat mean here? | A stick used to hit the ball | To show surprise | *To take a turn at hitting the ball | A small flying animal
exam: Which meaning of bat fits best in «Bats are mammals, not birds, and most eat insects or fruit»? | To show no surprise | A stick for hitting a ball | To take a turn at hitting the ball | *A small flying animal
